🛒 Online Shop – Hackathon Phase 1 Submission
📌 Project Overview

This project is a web-based Online Shop application, developed and deployed as part of Hackathon Phase 1.
It demonstrates expertise in Git & GitHub, Linux, and Docker, focusing on efficient repository management, Linux command usage, and Docker containerization.
🚀 Key Features

    Frontend: React (Built with Vite)
    Version Control: Managed using Git & GitHub
    Deployment: Dockerized using Docker & Docker Compose
    Web Server: Nginx
    Hackathon Topics Covered: Linux, Git & GitHub, Docker

🛠 Task Descriptions & Implementations
1️⃣ Repository Management (Git & GitHub)

    Forked the given repository to my GitHub account.
    Created a new branch (fix/docker-build) for modifications and feature enhancements.
    Used Git commands for proper version control:

git clone https://github.com/talhaaziz8/online_shop.git  
git checkout -b fix/docker-build  
git add .  
git commit -m "Added Docker support and Nginx configuration"  
git push origin fix/docker-build  

    Created a pull request (PR) for merging changes back to the main repository.

2️⃣ Linux Commands & Scripts Used

    File and Directory Management:

ls  
cd  
mkdir  
rm -rf  

Permissions & Execution:

chmod +x script.sh  

Networking & System Commands:

    curl -I http://localhost  
    ps aux | grep node  
    docker ps -a  

🛠 Git & GitHub Workflow

1️⃣ Clone the Repository (If you haven't already)

git clone https://github.com/talhaaziz8/online_shop.git  

2️⃣ Check the Current Branch

git branch  

3️⃣ Switch to the Correct Branch (if needed)

git checkout <your-branch-name>  

4️⃣ Make Changes & Commit

git add .  
git commit -m "Updated README with GitHub and Docker Hub info"  

5️⃣ Push Changes to GitHub

git push origin <your-branch-name>  

📦 Docker Image on Docker Hub

You can pull and run the Docker image directly from Docker Hub:

1️⃣ Pull the Image

docker pull talhaaziz/my-app:latest  

2️⃣ Run the Container

docker run -d -p 80:80 talhaaziz/my-app  

👉 Docker Hub Repository: talhaaziz/my-app
🛠 Installation & Setup (Docker - Local Build & Run)

1️⃣ Clone the Repository

git clone https://github.com/talhaaziz8/online_shop.git  

2️⃣ Build & Run with Docker Compose

docker-compose up -d --build  

3️⃣ Access the Application

Once running, open your browser and go to:

👉 http://localhost
3️⃣ Docker Integration & Deployment

I containerized the application using Docker and automated the setup using Docker Compose.
🏗 Dockerfile (Multi-stage Build for React + Nginx)

# Stage 1: Build the React app  
FROM node:18 AS build  
WORKDIR /app  
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./  
RUN npm install  
COPY . .  
RUN npm run build  

# Stage 2: Serve the app using Nginx  
FROM nginx:alpine  
COPY --from=build /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html  
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf  
EXPOSE 80  
CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]  

📄 docker-compose.yaml (Automating the setup)

version: '3.8'  
services:  
  web:  
    build: .  
    ports:  
      - "80:80"  
    restart: always  
    volumes:  
      - ./nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf  

🌐 nginx.conf (Nginx configuration for serving React app)

server {  
    listen 80;  
    server_name localhost;  

    location / {  
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;  
        index index.html;  
        try_files $uri /index.html;  
    }  

    error_page 404 /404.html;  
    location = /404.html {  
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;  
    }  
}  

